  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A solid sphere of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span> and radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0\\; \\textup{m}\"></span>, initially at rest, takes <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span> seconds to roll down a ramp without slipping. The angular acceleration of the sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.25\\; \\textup{rad\\,s}^{-1}\"></span>. The moment of inertia for a solid sphere is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{2}{5}mr^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is the mass and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> is the radius of the sphere.</p>\n<p>What is the total kinetic energy of the sphere when it reaches the bottom of the ramp?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"80\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"140\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
